perience from the links below."}]}],["$","nav",null,{"className":"page-links","aria-label":"Find a portfolio page","children":[["$","a","/",{"className":"page-link","href":"/","children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Home"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Start with an introduction to my work."}]]}],["$","a","/research/",{"className":"page-link","href":"/research/","children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Research"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Explore my research agenda and publications."}]]}],["$","a","/teaching/",{"className":"page-link","href":"/teaching/","children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Teaching"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Read about my approach and experience."}]]}],["$","a","/about/cv/",{"className":"page-link","href":"/about/cv/","children":[["$","h2",null,{"children":"Curriculum vitae"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Read my full academic record."}]]}]]}]]}],"children":["$","$L19",null,{"children":["$","$L16",null,{"segmentMap":{"children":[]},"children":["$","$L17",null,{"id":"page:/teaching/assessment/"}]}]}]}]}]}]}]
1:[["$","div",null,{"className":"page-intro shell","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"eyebrow","children":"Teaching & supervision"}],["$","h1",null,{"children":"Using assessment to guide instruction."}],["$","div",null,{"className":"intro-copy","children":["$","p",null,{"children":"I am learning to connect assessment evidence with instructional decisions through graduate study in EDTL 3103. My focus is on selecting appropriate measures, interpreting progress, and explaining next steps clearly."}]}]]}],["$","nav",null,{"className":"section-tabs","aria-label":"Section pages","children":["$","div",null,{"className":"shell","children":[["$","a","overview",{"href":"/teaching","aria-current":"$undefined","children":"Overview"}],["$","a","philosophy",{"href":"/teaching/philosophy/","aria-current":"$undefined","children":"Teaching Philosophy"}],["$","a","iowa",{"href":"/teaching/iowa/","aria-current":"$undefined","children":"Teaching at Iowa"}],["$","a","penn-state",{"href":"/teaching/penn-state/","aria-current":"$undefined","children":"Teaching at Penn State"}],["$","a","schools",{"href":"/teaching/schools/","aria-current":"$undefined","children":"School Experience"}],["$","a","assessment",{"href":"/teaching/assessment/","aria-current":"page","children":"Assessment & Planning"}],["$","a","reflection",{"href":"/teaching/reflection/","aria-current":"$undefined","children":"Reflective Practice"}]]}]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"shell","children":[false,false,false,false,false,false,false,["$","section",null,{"className":"content-section","children":[["$","span",null,{"className":"status-badge","children":"Graduate coursework · EDTL 3103 · Fall 2026"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"wide-prose","children":[["$","p",null,{"children":"My coursework in Assessment, Instructional Planning, and Practice develops my ability to connect assessment evidence with instructional decisions. I am examining how brief measures, error analysis, and repeated progress monitoring can guide support while accounting for learners’ opportunities to learn, language backgrounds, and access needs."}],["$","p",null,{"children":"This work complements my preparation in special education and behavior analysis by asking what a score can tell us, what additional information is needed, and how assessment should inform the next instructional step."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"grid-two","children":[["$","article",null,{"className":"info-card","children":[["$","h3",null,{"children":"Choosing evidence for the decision"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Assessment begins with a question about learning. I distinguish curriculum-based assessments of taught content from curriculum-based measures used to sample skills and monitor progress. Screening, instructional planning, progress monitoring, and diagnostic assessment serve different purposes."}]]}],["$","article",null,{"className":"info-card","children":[["$","h3",null,{"children":"From scoring to interpretation"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Early literacy, numeracy, and mathematics examples help me examine administration and scoring choices. Number identification, quantity discrimination, and missing-number tasks sample different skills. Reading examples add letter naming and nonsense-word fluency. Interpretation requires distinguishing rate from accuracy, comparing progress with goals, and following each measure’s scoring rules."}]]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"wide-prose section-space","children":[["$","h3",null,{"children":"Connecting assessment with support"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Within multi-tiered systems of support (MTSS), assessment informs instructional intensity. Data-based individualization connects progress monitoring, error analysis, instructional adaptation, and further monitoring. Powell and Stecker (2014) illustrate this iterative process in mathematics intervention."}],["$","p",null,{"children":"I am also developing ways to explain results clearly to families, including why an instructional-level measure may be useful without describing a learner as fixed at a particular grade or developmental level."}]]}],"$L1a","$L1b","$L1c","$L1d"]}]]}]]
1a:["$","figure",null,{"className":"assessment-cycle","aria-labelledby":"assessment-cycle-title","children":[["$","figcaption",null,{"children":[["$","h3",null,{"id":"assessment-cycle-title","children":"From evidence to instructional decisions"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"An organizing sequence for my learning in assessment and instructional planning."}]]}],["$","ol",null,{"children":[["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Define the decision"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Identify the learning question and the support being considered."}]]}],["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Examine the evidence"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Interpret scores, error patterns, and opportunities to learn."}]]}],["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Adapt instruction"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Connect the evidence with a specific instructional response."}]]}],["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Monitor and revisit"}],["$","span",null,{"children":"Review progress and reconsider the support provided."}]]}]]}]]}]
1b:["$","div",null,{"className":"table-scroll","children":["$","table",null,{"children":[["$","thead",null,{"children":["$","tr",null,{"children":[["$","th",null,{"children":"Learning focus"}],["$","th",null,{"children":"Application in my preparation"}]]}]}],["$","tbody",null,{"children":[["$","tr","Assessment purpose",{"children":[["$","td",null,{"children":"Assessment purpose"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"Match the measure to the question and instructional decision."}]]}],["$","tr","Administration & scoring",{"children":[["$","td",null,{"children":"Administration & scoring"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"Follow standardized directions and identify the scoring unit."}]]}],["$","tr","Data interpretation",{"children":[["$","td",null,{"children":"Data interpretation"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"Distinguish accuracy, rate, current performance, and growth."}]]}],["$","tr","Instructional response",{"children":[["$","td",null,{"children":"Instructional response"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"Use error patterns and progress data to consider adaptations."}]]}],["$","tr","Family communication",{"children":[["$","td",null,{"children":"Family communication"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"Explain results and next steps in accessible language."}]]}],["$","tr","Fairness",{"children":[["$","td",null,{"children":"Fairness"}],["$","td",null,{"children":"Consider language, learning history, opportunity, and access."}]]}]]}]]}]}]
1c:["$","div",null,{"className":"reflection","children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"What I am learning"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Accurate measurement is necessary, but its value depends on the decisions it supports. I want to interpret patterns across observations, consider the conditions under which learners perform, and communicate both the usefulness and the limits of the evidence."}]]}]
1d:["$","div",null,{"className":"source-note","children":[["$","h3",null,{"children":"Course foundations"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"This page reflects graduate study in EDTL 3103, including CBA, CBM, MTSS, early numeracy, mathematics assessment, and data-based individualization. The instructor’s slides, lecture transcripts, assigned textbook chapters, and quizzes inform this reflection."}],["$","p",null,{"children":["Powell, S. R., & Stecker, P. M. (2014). Using data-based individualization to intensify mathematics intervention for students with disabilities. ",["$","em",null,{"children":"Teaching Exceptional Children, 46"}],"(4), 31–37. ",["$","a",null,{"className":"text-link","href":"https://doi.org/10.1177/0040059914523735","target":"_blank","rel":"noreferrer","children":"Publisher record"}]]}]]}]
